<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Datum cut to neutral.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Datum cut to neutral.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Rodman &amp; Renshaw Inc said Tuesday it downgraded Datum Inc to neutral from buy.</p>
<p>-- Rodman said it had reinstated a buy on the stock on April 7 at $16 a share. On Monday, the stock set a record high of $27.75 a share. Rodman's price target was $27 a share or 18.6 times its 1998 earnings per share estimate of $1.45.</p>
<p>-- Rodman said it also has concerns about the company's backlog of orders, which declined by $4.2 milion in the first quarter.</p>
<p>-- Datum shares were off $0.75 at $25.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
